.TH WREX-SLL2 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-sll2 \- sll2 layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIsll2\fR \fB--sll2\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIsll2\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
Linux cooked capture v2 (LINKTYPE_LINUX_SLL2): 20\-byte pseudo\-header — protocol u16 FIRST, reserved u16, ifindex u32, hatype u16, pkttype/halen u8, 8\-byte address region. A root layer (rank 10); protocol drives the chain like eth.type.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 10 (valid stack start: no parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --sll2-protocol).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-sll2\-protocol=\fIINT\fR\fR
encapsulated ethertype (autofill: derived from next layer) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-sll2\-reserved=\fIINT\fR\fR
reserved (0) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-sll2\-ifindex=\fIINT\fR\fR
1\-based interface index the frame arrived on Type u32. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-sll2\-hatype=\fIINT\fR\fR
link\-layer address type (bare ARP hardware code) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-sll2\-pkttype=\fIINT\fR\fR
packet type: host|broadcast|multicast|otherhost|outgoing or a bare 0\-4 number Type str. Default: host.
.TP
\fB\-\-sll2\-halen=\fIINT\fR\fR
link\-layer address length in bytes (autofill: 6) Type u8. Default: 6.
.TP
\fB\-\-sll2\-addr\fR
link\-layer address (8\-byte region; MACs occupy the low 6) Type bytes. Default: .

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex fields sll2

